\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee ends firm, RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in forwards. \b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, March 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended Tuesday stronger against the dollar in both spot and forward markets. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market in a limited way to moderate the rupee's gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended at 39.515/525 per dollar against its Monday close of 39.535/545. \par \par \uc2  "Corporates are expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be stable for some time and there is little demand," a private bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Even the State Bank of India (SBI), India's largest commercial bank, was not very active today," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended stronger against the forward dollar as sentiment on the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was strong after the RBI moved to improve liquidity and signal lower interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI on Monday said it will cut banks' CRR to 10 percent from 10.5 in two slabs of 25 basis points each, effective March 28 and April 11. Last week it cut its repo rate to eight percent from nine and the key bank rate to 10.5 percent from 11. \par \par \uc2  "Corporate volumes were very poor, since they are waiting for lower rates," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI has been signalling an easy money policy which is causing expectations of softer forward dollar premiums also," he said. \par \par \uc2  Forward dollar premiums fell by around 20 paise (0.2 rupee) on Monday in trade after the official close after the RBI's announcement of cuts in banks' CRR. \par \par \uc2  Premiums opened down on Tuesday and were weak through the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI did sell-buy swaps for April-dollars in what dealers described as "passive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was through outright forward dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  "RBI was not very active, they did deals with banks who went to them," a dealer said. "Their actions were aimed more at checking volatility in the market than setting levels." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the RBI also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March-dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with some profit-taking by banks, caused premiums to firm up slightly from opening levels," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The annualised premium on six-month dollars ended at 7.27 percent against the previous close of 7.69, after hitting an inntra-day low of 6.95 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08smc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
