\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee slides, market awaits RBI support. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit a month-low on Monday as lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coupled with an uncertain political situation and a regional downtrend in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets triggered a rush for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after 1300 local time (0730 GMT), the rupee was quoted at around 39.16/20, down from Friday's 38.92/95. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the slide in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  added to the pressure, but the main factor driving trade on Monday was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's absence from the market since Friday when the rupee was at the psychological barrier of 38.90 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Once the rupee went past 38.90 on Friday and the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think corporates got jittery," the chief dealer at an American bank said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market perceived the rupee overvalued at its present level but said it had been held there by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tough defence. \par \par \uc2  Last month, when the rupee touched a historic low of 40.45 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reacted by raising its bank rate by 200 basis points to 11 percent. \par \par \uc2  It also tightened liquidity by raising reserve requirements. \par \par \uc2  The firm defence had propped up the rupee but the RBI's absence from the market on Friday and market talk that the bank was under pressure from industry to lower interest rates had sent the market scurrying for dollars again, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI's measures only bottled up demand. It was lying there waiting to be triggered off," said J Moses Harding, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Indusind Bank. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said uncertainty over the electoral verdict in ongoing polls had also contributed to the rupee's weakness. \par \par \uc2  "I think it is becoming clear that we will have a hung parliament," he said. "And this is worrying some corporates." \par \par \uc2  Monday was the third day of voting in India's second election in as many years in a staggered schedule which runs until March 7. Two snowbound constituencies vote in June. \par \par \uc2  Opinion polls have said no single party will get a majority, forcing another coalition government. \par \par \uc2  "This throws up a whole host of problems for India," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "We have to look at a slowdown in policy-making which in turn will affect the economy." \par \par \uc2  Traders said if the rupee breached the 39.20 level, it could slide to 40. But they hoped the RBI would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before that. \par \par \uc2  Another factor putting pressure on the rupee was the fall of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Monday after a meeting of G7 finance ministers failed to announce new moves to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "At the moment it is not very clear whether the south and east Asian economies are out of the woods," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee will have to weaken to maintain our export competitiveness if other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee has weakened around nine percent since the Asian turmoil began while some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Indonesian rupiah have dropped by more than 70 percent. \par \par \uc2  Even regional heavyweight Singapore has seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed more than 12 percent of its value in the same period. \par \par \uc2  Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699 \par \par \uc2  Email -- Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2n01ces\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
