\par\par \b \uc2  India Call Rate Ends Up On Lenders Pushing For Higher Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1998\par 11:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian interbank overnight call rate closed higher Tuesday because lenders pushed for higher call rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The call rate closed between 9.25% and 10.00%, higher than its Monday close of between 8.75% and 9.50%. \par \par \uc2  The call rate was briefly traded at 10.00% and 10.50% in afternoon trades, 'but after the afternoon check clearances of banks the call was traded lower at around 9.25% and 10.00%,' said a primary dealer. \par \par \uc2  He said the call rate isn't expected to rise substantially this week despite the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap market by paying rupee premiums for forward dollars. \par \par \uc2  The RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market via swap deals to absorb rupees and stop the dollar from rising to the INR39.00 mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the primary dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow from the sale of fixed-rate three-day repurchase agreements of government securities held by the RBI earlier Tuesday was only INR620 million, lower than the INR9.87 billion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  received Monday. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the INR9.87 billion will be flowing back to the banking system Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a large mutual fund who confirmed lending money at around 10.25% said the call rate could be firmer next week if the RBI continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and absorb rupees. \par \par \uc2  The call rate had risen to between 40% and 100% after Jan. 16 because of the RBI's measures to reduce liquidity in the banking system and stop speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'If the RBI feels that there is once again excess rupees in the system then they may decide to reduce liquidity,' said the primary dealer. \par \par \uc2  For indicative call rates please see Dow Jones Markets page [57435]. \par \par \uc2  -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya; (91-22) 288-4211 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-02-98 \par \par \uc2  1026GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2300wgh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
