\par\par \b \uc2  India Call Rates Ends Lower On More Than Enough Money \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1998\par 11:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian interbank overnight call rate closed lower Monday on more than enough money available in the banking system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last two weeks has released significant rupee funds into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  The call rate closed Monday between 8.75% and 9.50%, lower than its Saturday close of between 8.00% and 10.00%. \par \par \uc2  The call rate was higher, however, in morning trades since large financial institutions weren't lending money as they waited for rates to rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But, 'with no major pressure for rupee funds from banks, financial institutions started lending money at around 9.50% in afternoon trades,' said a primary dealer. \par \par \uc2  The liquidity in the market was indicated by the RBI receiving 9.86 billion rupees (INR) of applications to its fixed-rate three-day repurchase agreements (RPs) of government securities earlier Monday. \par \par \uc2  On Saturday, the RBI had received only INR300 million of applications at its RP auction. \par \par \uc2  However, 'the call rate could slightly open higher at around 10.00% on Tuesday,' said the primary dealer. \par \par \uc2  He explained that lenders will try for higher call rates at the opening because of the outflows to RPs. \par \par \uc2  The call rate had risen to trade over 40.00% for the last two weeks following the RBI's decision to raise its bank rate, cut refinance facilities to banks, and raise banks' cash reserve ratio to reduce liquidity in the banking system and stop speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But a dealer at a large lending institution said that the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has released significant rupees into the banking system over the last two weeks. \par \par \uc2  According to the RBI's weekly data, the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings rose by $369 million to $27.118 billion in the week ended Jan. 23. \par \par \uc2  The increase was mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases, thereby releasing rupees, from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  For indicative call rates please see Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya; (91-22) 288-4211 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-02-98 \par \par \uc2  1012GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2200v0x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
