\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 /RBI/Cool Rates -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected In Feb \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 14:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said call rates could rise once again over 100% Saturday and next week as banks will have only four trading days to meet their cash reserve requirements. Monday and Friday are trading holidays. \par \par \uc2  Currently the sentiment in the money market is bad and the call rate is high because of panic among banks and lenders refusing to lend money at lower levels, said a dealer at a U.S. bank. He said the high call has led to speculation in the money market by companies. \par \par \uc2  He explained that companies are buying commercial paper at high yields from banks who in turn are lending the rupees received by companies in the call money market at high levels. \par \par \uc2  The yields on the commercial papers have doubled to between 20% and 25%, he said. \par \par \uc2  There is lot of panic and speculation in the money market and the call rate will come down with a little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the RBI because 'there aren't any major outflows from the banking system until the advance-tax outflows at end-March,' said Ashish Parthasarthi, chief of money market at HDFC Bank Ltd. \par \par \uc2  The RBI cannot shift the problem in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to the domestic money market, said a senior dealer at state-owned Dena Bank. \par \par \uc2  If they don't reverse some of the measures or don't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  then 'the sky is the limit for the call rate,' said the dealer at the U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The primary dealer said that the RBI isn't likely to cut banks' cash reserve ratio or reverse its other measures because it would lead the market to believe that the RBI is comfortable with the situation and again lead to speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The RBI won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately because they don't want the problem to resurface in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said the primary dealer. \par \par \uc2  'The correction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has to look enduring and the best way to deal with the situation is via repurchase transaction wherein the banks requiring rupees get financed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya; (91-22) 288-4211 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1330GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1n00nph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
