\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus: India Rupee Falls To Record Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Pankaj Aher \par \uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1998\par 12:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee fell to an all-time low against the dollar Wednesday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and traders said only a spurt in dollar inflows can keep the rupee from falling further over the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rupee opened lower on early demand for dollars from banks, and quickly broke through its record low of INR 39.95 to the dollar with no sign of any large dollar sellers in the market. \par \par \uc2  After the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when that low was broken, the market quickly took the rupee below the key level of INR 40.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Market players had expected at least the State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank, to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupee's fall. But it too stayed away. It has sold dollars over the last week and the market's perception is that those sales were at the behest of the RBI. \par \par \uc2  Eventually, the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold dollars in two rounds. Those sales effectively prevented the rupee from falling below 40.20 to the dollar, helping it close between INR 40.10 and INR 40.15, versus INR 39.86-.89 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Although analysts said they expect the rupee to continue to fall, senior government officials tried to downplay Wednesday's drop. \par \par \uc2  'This is a minor adjustment and the RBI is watching the situation for any excess volatility,' Indian Finance Secretary Montek Singh Ahluwalia told Dow Jones Wednesday. 'There is no reason to be alarmed,' \par \par \uc2  Ahluwalia also said the rupee's fall has to be viewed in the backdrop of the fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values across Southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1152GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 62553 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1e00bgm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
