\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee revisits record low, aims 40/dlr level. \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee on Tuesday touched a new record closing rate against the dollar for the second successive day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The spot rupee revisted its record traded low of 39.93 to the dollar before dollar sales by the State Bank of India (SBI) helped it recover to close at 39.88/90, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had closed Monday at 39.81/83, its previous lowest closing rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's weakening continued on the back of rising corporate dollar demand and dwindling supplies, they said. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers said they expected the rupee to hit the 40 per dollar level soon. \par \par \uc2  "There was steady demand for dollars throughout the day," said a foriegn bank dealer. "We might see the rupee trading at a new horizon in couple of days -- might be tomorrow," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The long awaited 40 per dollar level might face the acid test tomorrow," a dealer at a brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  "SBI is the only one to supply sedative in a sliding market," a foreign bank dealer said, referring to SBI's dollar sales. The state-run SBI is India's leading commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  "We might not see a dramatic down fall of the rupee in the next few days but it will steadily slip," a dealer said \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee's weakening on Tuesday was a matter of concern as most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged a recovery which was not reflected in the local market. \par \par \uc2  The rupee saw a traded high of 39.83 and a low of 39.93 on Tuesday, with majority of the deals struck within the 39.85-39.90 range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had hit a lifetime low of 39.93 on December 16, but strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped it recover. \par \par \uc2  The rupee weakened in the forward dollar market on Tuesday but a steep fall was averted by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swap market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market had started discounting the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swap market which have become regular in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is yielding diminishing returns as the market had discounted it and a hungry market absorbed all the supplies, dealers said. Only massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could make a difference, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Compared to the steady one way slide in the spot market, the the forward dollar market saw two way movement. \par \par \uc2  The six month dollar premiums closed at 10.50 percent compared to its previous close of 10.24 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07xuw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
