\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in swap market-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through swap deals on late morning trade Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They (the RBI) were in July maturity deals," a dealer at a public sector bank said. \par \par \uc2  Premiums fell across the board after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "July dollars are now quoted at 2.08/2.15 rupees from the opening level of 2.15/2.19," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Premiums had opened up on Tuesday on rising corporate demand for forward dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The spot rupee was weakening gradually. \par \par \uc2  The spot rupee was quoted at 39.87/90 to the dollar at 11.25 a.m. (0555 GMT) compared with the previous close of 39.81/83. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Tuesday at 39.82/85 to the dollar. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07xr9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
