\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Indian rupee at lowest closing rate vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sudhir Shetty \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Rising dollar demand from Indian firms in the wake of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks meltdown and dwindling supplies dragged the rupee to its lowest ever closing rate on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "That the rupee is  weakening almost by 10 paise (0.10 rupees) a day is a matter of concern," said Moses Harding, chief dealer at IndusInd Bank, leading private bank. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the rupee closed at 39.81/83 per dollar, its lowest ever closing rate, slipping past the previous record close of 39.74/76 hit on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been among the least affected \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, falling by only around 10 percent against the dollar since August 1997. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had hit a record traded low of 39.93 on December 16, but aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) had propped it up. \par \par \uc2  "It is purely corporate dollar demand," said a dealer at a French bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  He said the rupee's current weakness faithfully mirrored the dollar supply demand mismatch as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week disallowed banks from taking speculative positions, thereby snuffing out interbank speculation. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a leading foreign bank said the rupee would hit the 40 per dollar level in the next few trading days if the current trend continued unchecked. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee is continuously under pressure as corporate dollar demand is rising and supply dwindling," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers attributed the rising corporate dollar demand to worries that the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meltdown would eventually lead to a further weakening of the Indian rupee. \par \par \uc2  Share prices in Bombay exchanges closed sharply lower on the back of worsening Asian economic woes, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) top 30-share index slumped 3.83 percent or 135.16 points to 3,395.04 points. \par \par \uc2  Portfolio investment by foreign institutional investors (FIIs) fell by $4.7 million in January 1-8, the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The market regulator said net FII investments dropped by $155.4 million in December, the second straight month of net outflows as foreign investors pulled out of the troubled region. \par \par \uc2  The only dollar suppliers in recent months have been either the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the state-run State Bank of India (SBI). \par \par \uc2  "At present, SBI is the only major dollar supplier in the market," said one dealer. "The rupee's sharp fall has been averted by SBI's supplies." \par \par \uc2  The RBI did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market on Monday, but was a large player in the forward dollar market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, July and August maturities in the swap market on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Premiums fell across the board on the impact of dollar sales by the RBI and SBI. Six-month dollar premiums closed at 10.24 percent compared with a weekend close of 10.84 percent. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1c07wd3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
