\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Slightly Lower In Early Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 05:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee (INR) opened higher against the dollar Friday but fell immediately and is trading slightly below its previous closing levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Friday at INR39.61-39.66. It rose immediately and was traded at INR39.71. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is trading at INR39.68-39.71 at 0350 GMT (10:50 p.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a few banks sold dollars at higher levels, causing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall back slightly. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are divided on whether the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  While a few dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee from falling further sharply, others said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could use other methods to cool the market. \par \par \uc2  One favorite theory in the market is that the State Bank of India trades on behalf of the RBI several times. 'You may see State Banks selling today, not RBI selling,' a dealer at a large European bank said. \par \par \uc2  State Bank is the country's largest commercial bank and its actions often set the trend for the market because it deals on behalf of several large corporates including state-owned oil companies. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes have fallen substantially since Wednesday after the RBI directed banks to hold square or near square positions at the end of trading everyday until further notice. The measure was aimed at easing the downward pressure on the rupee a major part of which the RBI believes was caused by interbank speculation. \par \par \uc2  The rupee traded at a record low of INR39.95 to the dollar on Dec. 2. \par \par \uc2  'We have to wait and see what happens, we are going with the market,' a dealer at a state-owned bank said. \par \par \uc2  There was substantial corporate demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, he noted. 'I think that demand will continue.' \par \par \uc2  Thursday, the forward premiums rose sharply on news that Moody's Investor Services would review for a possible downgrade India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds and deposits ratings. \par \par \uc2  The premium for benchmark July dollars closed Thursday between INR2.50 and INR2.60, up from INR1.85-1.88 at the close of trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  For the latest indicative rupee rates, please see Dow Jones page [26501]. \par \par \uc2  -By Pankaj Aher; (91-22) 288-4211; paher@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0410GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du19006oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
