\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee bows under rising dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee came under renewed pressure on Tuesday, unsettled by rising dollar demand from industry and the impact of wilting Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic dollar sales by the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI) and a token \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) with one Bombay bank could only temporarily halt the rupee's slide, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee saw a traded low of 39.62 to the dollar compared with 39.42/45 at the opening and a previous close of 39.41/43. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a major reason behind the rise in dollar demand appeared to be a revival in industrial activity. \par \par \uc2  "What we saw in December was a lull in industrial activity," said a foreign bank dealer. "The dollar demand reflects the revival of activity in several industries," he said. \par \par \uc2  Another reason for the spurt in dollar demand was the travel requirement of Haj pilgrims who go to Moslem's holiest city of Mecca in Saudi Arabia, a dealer at a public sector bank said. \par \par \uc2  "This is the Haj season and they need to carry dollars," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has weakened around nine percent since August, 1997. \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit an historic low of 39.90 to the dollar on December 2, 1997, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to launch a rescue package. \par \par \uc2  The RBI tightened domestic liquidity and hiked export credit in late 1997 with a view to prevent diversion of cheap rupees to fund speculation and encourage faster repatriation of export proceeds by Indian exporters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steps brought calm to the market and in late December it began rolling back some of its measures. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the withdrawal was a little too early as free falling South-east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have created apprehensions of a domino effect on the rupee," Societe Generale bank said in an India report. \par \par \uc2  "With dollar on the rampage against major (Asian) \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , corporates are likely to be nervous to hold short dollar positions," the report said. \par \par \uc2  Forward dollar premiums also flared up on Tuesday, reflecting the rupee's weakness in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  One year dollar premiums were quoted at 8.50 percent on Tuesday afternoon compared to the previous close of 7.88 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The overseas NDF (non-deliverable forward) market is retesting an all-time high of 44.70 (rupees to the dollar) for one year forward with premium quoted at 5.35 rupees," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The NDF market is mainly patronised by foreign institutional investors who are not allowed to hedge their Indian equities exposures within India. \par \par \uc2  The chief dealer at a foreign bank said the rupee would hit the 40 per dollar mark by March. \par \par \uc2  "It could happen much earlier," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du1601a3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
