\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee slips, breaches 39.50 per dollar-level. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The rupee breached the 39.50 to the dollar level within minutes of the market opening on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Things are not so good for the rupee with South-east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  passing through all-time lows," said Moses Harding, chief dealer at the private IndusInd Bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Tuesday at 39.42/45 against the dollar compared with the previous close of 39.41/43. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee should continue to slip unless the RBI (the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market for about a month, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It has been focusing on the forward dollar market, where its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped halt a rise in premiums, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the rupee fell to 39.42 compared with the weekend low of 39.31/32. \par \par \uc2  "It means it has closed around 20 paise weaker (on Monday) compared to the year end close despite RBI showing its concern by token \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said IndusInd's Harding. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du1601a1z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
