\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee exchange rate band inappropriate-RBI. \b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 25 (Reuters) - An exchange rate band for the Indian rupee is inappropriate in the current circumstances, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Thursday in its "Report on \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance 1996-97". \par \par \uc2  The RBI said stabilising the rupee-dollar exchange rate continues to be an important factor guiding exchange rate policy. But it rejected suggestions that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band could be set as a stabiliser. \par \par \uc2  "In view of the complexities involved in exactly identifying the course of the equilibrium rate, there is a suggestion for use of bands to represent fundamentals, but this would be inappropriate on credibility grounds," the RBI's report said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has fallen around nine percent against the U.S. dollar since mid-August, ending Wednesday at 39.16/18 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The RBI stopped the rupee breaking through the 40-mark earlier this month by erecting a defence package. This includes forcing up short-term interest rates, speeding up exporters remittances and making imports of non-essential goods more costly. \par \par \uc2  The RBI also spent nearly $2.5 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall since the end of October. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's decline started in August when a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overvalued on a trade-weighted basis after the rupee had held firm for a year against a dollar. \par \par \uc2  There were also media reports in August that Indian authorities were considering introducing an exchange rate band. Despite subsequent denials by authorities, the idea occasionally bobbed up during the rupee's recent volatility. \par \par \uc2  An expert group set up earlier this year to chart a phased move to capital account convertibility had recommended a band of five percent above or below the neutral real effective exchange rate (REER). The group proposed that this would happen once the rupee was made convertible on the capital account, which is planned in the next few years. \par \par \uc2  REER measures a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance against those of major trading partners taking into account differentials in inflation rates, interest rates, productivity, financial asset values and several other components. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's fortunes have largely depended on the ebb and flow of foreign capital coming into \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Until last August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to buy dollars to stop the rupee firming beyond 35.70. \par \par \uc2  The RBI bought $7.8 billion in 1996/97, and up until the end of October was still a dollar buyer. But when capital inflows dried up in the wake of the market crisis in Asia, the RBI turned into a heavy dollar seller as the rupee's fall accelerated. \par \par \uc2  It said a band can be based on REER, but constructing REER indicators is fraught with difficulties. As it only takes the trade account into its reckoning it would not represent all the fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Developments in capital flows also had to be factored into policy making, although they should not be the sole determining factor, the RBI said. \par \par \uc2  "In the face of large destabilising capital flows and/or periodic deviation from norms suggested as pre-conditions, rigid pursuance of such a band could however be costly and disruptive," the RBI cautioned. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcp00ovl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
