\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends at 39.27/30 per dlr, off 39.90. \b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended Tuesday at a new record low of 39.27/30 per dollar, slightly weaker than its previous close of 39.25/30 but off an intraday low of 39.90 hit in morning trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the rupee weakened on strong dollar demand from banks which bought ahead of anticipated demand from corporates and rapidly fell to a lifetime low of 39.90 in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee appreciated later on news of RBI's package of measures to support the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "When this news was known to the market, speculators began to back off," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "There was also profit-taking from players holding dollars." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee rallied to around 39.50 levels when a large state-run bank sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Then the RBI announced its package and the rupee bounced to to 39.10/17 levels," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's package along with expectations of dollar inflows from a global depositary (GDR) issue by a leading state-run firm could help the rupee stabilise after a fall of around 10.0 percent in just over three months. \par \par \uc2  The GDR issue by the Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited (MTNL) is expected to raise around $370 million. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the rupee to stabilise on the MTNL factor and the package," said a dealer at a private bank. "But how long this will last remains to be seen." \par \par \uc2  "The rupee is likely to come back under pressure unless RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the RBI was placing excessive emphasis on the speculation factor. \par \par \uc2  "There is some pretty strong demand from corporates and this will have to be met from somewhere," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The package of measures announced by the RBI included steps to tighten liquidity and raise short term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  But the move to tighten liquidity pushed up forward premiums, weakening the rupee against the forward dollar. \par \par \uc2  Premiums rose 10-15 paise across all maturities but ended little changed from Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Among the measures announced by RBI on Tuesday were a hike in banks' cash reserve ratio (CRR) to 10.0 percent from 9.5 percent and in interest on repos to 5.0 percent from 4.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it was holding in abeyance a planned reduction in the CRR announced in a credit policy statement in October. The RBI had scheduled a series of cuts announced to bring the CRR down from 10 percent to eight percent by March. \par \par \uc2  These moves superseded a milder support package announced last Friday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The RBI also said it was removing a 10 percent incremental CRR on non-resident rupee deposits. \par \par \uc2  "This move is an attempt to get banks to canvass more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts," said a dealer. "It should help in improving inflows to some extent." \par \par \uc2  The RBI also said authorised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers needed to see customers' evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure before offering forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had come under mounting pressure as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows dried up in the aftermath of the Asian markets crisis and Indian firms exhausting their external commercial borrowing limits. \par \par \uc2  A perception that the rupee needed to depreciate to take into account the dramatic falls in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar also gripped the market. \par \par \uc2  And a political crisis culminating in the fall of the United Front coalition government on Friday piled on the speculative pressure. \par \par \uc2  Indian political parties on Tuesday were still trying to cobble together a new coalition, otherwise the country faces fresh elections. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc201tsz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
