\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee weaker,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears limits scope. \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was weaker against both the spot and forward dollar in late morning trade Monday and dealers said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had checked a sharper fall. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say political uncertainty, after prime minister Inder Kumar Gujral resigned on Friday, gives fodder to speculators, but fear of heavy RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped a sharp move so far. \par \par \uc2  No single party or political bloc commands absolute majority in India's parliament and a snap poll is likely, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody is quite sure when Reserve Bank of India (RBI) will come in," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "Corporates are keeping off the market at the moment to see what RBI will do. There are no bids above 38.80." \par \par \uc2  "The rupee has broadly traded in 38.70-38.80 per dollar range so far," he said. "There have been stray deals at 38.68 and 38.81." \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit a record low of 38.85 per dollar on Friday before rallying to close at 38.55/58 on Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Later on Friday, RBI announced a package of measures to speed up inward remittances of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by exporters and to mop up excess domestic liquidity to prevent banks using the extra funds to speculate in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said RBI had checked for prices in the morning. \par \par \uc2  "They have been prowling around, checking out prices," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "But so far there has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "But RBI will have to come in soon," he said. \par \par \uc2  "If they stay off the market for another hour or so, then I think corporates may start buying," the dealer said. "And pressure will then start building for a test of 39." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward premiums had risen on corporate demand. \par \par \uc2  "There has been some booking of forward cover in near months in particular," said a dealer. "Premiums are up across the board largely in reaction to the weakening in spot. The prospect of a tightening in domestic liquidity has also hit sentiment." \par \par \uc2  The premium for six-month dollars was quoted at 7.42 percent in late morning against the weekend close of 6.51 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc101rc2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
