\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee weakens vs forward dlr, RBI stays away. \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 28 (Reuters) -  The Indian rupee weakened further against the forward dollar in afternoon trade Friday as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to materialise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through swaps, a regular feature of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days, but had not done so on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Their (RBI) absence is driving premiums up," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "There is some dollar demand -- mainly interbank and some from corporates." \par \par \uc2  At 2 p.m.(0830 GMT), the annualised premium on six-month forward dollars was 6.75 percent against Thursday's close of 6.02 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Normally there is some demand from banks towards the end of every month when they roll over swaps, particularly on their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But it also looks like some banks are taking fresh positions besides squaring off existing ones." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said repeated RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market had helped the rupee settle down after high volatility in the morning when it hit a record low of 38.85 minutes after opening. \par \par \uc2  At 2 p.m. (0830 GMT), the rupee was quoted 38.58/62 per dollar against its previous close of 38.60/63. \par \par \uc2  "The market is moving up and down with the RBI," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "Volumes are thin and there is nothing much other than RBI to move the market today." \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 