\par\par \b \uc2  Safety net arrives for rupee as government teeters. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Simon Cameron-Moore \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par 18:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 28 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a package on Friday to prop up the ailing rupee but even as it acted the country's government faced collapse, raising the prospect of more pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Sources in the governing coalition said Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral's resignation was imminent after the opposition Congress party withdrew its support for his minority government. \par \par \uc2  The climax of the political drama came at the end of a day when the rupee had already plunged to all-time lows. \par \par \uc2  It hit a record of 38.85 per dollar, eight percent below mid-August levels, before a Reserve bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made for a half-hearted recovery. \par \par \uc2  The rupee closed at 38.55/59, a shade stronger than its previous close of 38.60/63, but dealers said strong dollar demand was still bubbling. \par \par \uc2  And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to take steps to curb speculation against the rupee and force Indian firms holding foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad to bring it home quickly. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers were sceptical whether the RBI package would have the desired effect, given the political denouement, and said it would have to come out with more measures. \par \par \uc2  The knock-on effect of the east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis pushed the rupee into a slide that gathered momentum in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The Congress party said it had withdrawn its make-or-break support to the United Front alliance of 15 parties and was staking a claim to form the next government. \par \par \uc2  However, no single political bloc now commands an absolute majority in parliament, raising the prospect of snap elections unless one group musters enough support to form a government. \par \par \uc2  Political uncertainty has been one of the factors driving speculation on the rupee, which the RBI says is a major cause for its recent fall. \par \par \uc2  Besides speeding up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remittances by exporters, the RBI's package of measures also aimed at tightening liquidity in the domestic money market to prevent banks using extra funds to speculate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would also call for details of cancellations of forward contracts above $500,000 since the beginning of the month. \par \par \uc2  It said it would monitor such cancellations in future to prevent speculation by firms which booked forward sales and cancelled them to take advantage of market turbulence. \par \par \uc2  "This will have a salutary effect on curbing volatility," said the chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a state-run bank. \par \par \uc2  "Many corporates -- including some big names -- have been speculating through cancellation of forward contracts." \par \par \uc2  In a related measure the RBI increased the interest rate on export credit to make it costlier for exporters to hold on to their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings. \par \par \uc2  The RBI also announced it would conduct repurchase auctions at a fixed rate of interest to mop up excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The RBI further said it would delay forthcoming cuts in banks' cash reserve ratio (CRR) requirements which it had announced in October. \par \par \uc2  But bankers were unconvinced the package would rescue the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they've done much to help the rupee, not after the government has fallen," said a dealer with a major foreign bank. "I think it will come under a fair amount of pressure on Monday morning." \par \par \uc2  Other bankers said the RBI had not exhausted all options. \par \par \uc2  "This is a shallow market and not a very developed one," said a dealer at a private bank. "If things go out of hand, the RBI will resort to its last option - massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood close to $26 billion on November 13. \par \par \uc2  Analysts estimate the reserves are enough to cover over seven months' imports and provide sufficient buffer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to beat back speculators. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbs01xa0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
