\par\par \b \uc2  Indian call money ends easy amid good liquidity. \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 26 (Reuters) - Indian call money ended Wednesday easier at 4.0-5.0 percent amid good liquidity compared to the previous close of 5.0-5.5 percent, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said call money rates eased in afternoon trade on good funds supply while demand petered out. \par \par \uc2  "There were few borrowers in the afternoon," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "Call money was steady for most of the morning and then easy." \par \par \uc2  The Mumbai Interbank Overnight Average Rate, a weighted-average of dealt rates from 15 banks and financial institutions, was 5.28 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said government bonds ended steady to slightly down in moderate trade with most of the traders keeping to the sidelines on uncertainty over the liquidity outlook. \par \par \uc2  They said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had led several traders to keep off the bond market in anticipation of a tightening in liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week and through this week to brake the rupee's fall against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the rupee ended at 38.55/60 per dollar, its lowest close, after hitting a record low of 38.70 in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  "So far the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not had much impact on the domestic money market," said a dealer. "This is because most of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have been through swaps." \par \par \uc2  The dealer said most of the active bond traders were also active players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "So they are a bit wary - they are the ones who are likely to be hit on the liquidity front if the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market hots up futher," he added. "Most of the trade at the moment is from players who are switching stocks." \par \par \uc2  The 12.59 percent 2004 bond closed at 108.77 rupees against its previous close of 108.80. \par \par \uc2  The 13.50 percent 1998 eased to 101.96 from 101.97. \par \par \uc2  The 10.85 percent 2001 was marginally down at 102.56 from 102.58. \par \par \uc2  Treasury bills were little changed with April bills steady at 7.45 percent and July bills inching up to 7.6 percent from 7.55. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbq01u31\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
