\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  RBI Sells -2: Small  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Has No Impact On Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1997\par 11:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of India sold dollars in the spot market just before the close of trading Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers at two foreign banks confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold them the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 1015 GMT (0415 am EST). \par \par \uc2  The RBI sold dollars around 37.45 rupees, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As reported, a dealer at one foreign bank had confirmed the RBI sold him dollars in late morning trading, but no other dealers could confirm that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1024 GMT (04:24 am EST) the dollar is trading between 37.42 rupees and 37.45 rupees. \par \par \uc2  'They are selling in small lots, so it has no impact on the market,' one of the dealers who transacted business with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  But most other dealers said the RBI hadn't approached them for trades. Several dealers said the RBI inquired about price-levels which caused the dollar to fall back a bit. \par \par \uc2  'There is no RBI,' a dealer at a state-owned bank said. 'People who are long dollars are selling now, that's why it's falling.' \par \par \uc2  One dealer estimated the RBI sold around $50 million to $70 million. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Wednesday between 37.43-.46 rupees, up from its close between 37.39-.41 rupees Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The rupee fell to a new 21-month low Tuesday at 37.52 to the dollar, but recovered on a statement by the Reserve Bank of India Governor C. Rangarajan that he believed 'the adjustment that has taken place in the value of the rupee is adequate.' \par \par \uc2  The RBI governor also said there wasn't any ground for a further weakening of the rupee in view of the strong fundamentals and added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any 'overshooting.' \par \par \uc2  For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [17960]. \par \par \uc2  -By Pankaj Aher; 91-22-2884211; paher@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1034GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbj08ug9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
