\par\par \b \uc2  India Spot Rupee Seen Opening Wed At 37.43; Range 37.30-.50 \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1997\par 04:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee is expected to quickly test the key support level of 37.50 when the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted Tuesday's steep slide in the rupee, halted by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , still hangs over the market. \par \par \uc2  The spot rupee is seen opening Wednesday around 37.43 and then trading in a range between 37.30-.50 during the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The key will be if the RBI shows itself and sells dollars around 37.50,' a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Bombay interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market commences at 0330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 GMT (5:30 am EST) close of trading Tuesday, the dollar was between 37.39-.41 rupees, up sharply from between 36.88-.89 rupees at the close of trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Tuesday between 36.91-.94 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded to a high of 37.52 rupees Tuesday. The last time the dollar traded around those levels was on February 7, 1996. It traded at an all time high of 38.40 rupees in intraday trading on February 6, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI sold an estimated $150 million in the spot market Tuesday after issuing a statement which stopped the fall of the rupee. But only two dealers could confirm having traded with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [17960]. \par \par \uc2  -By Ed Lane; (91-11) 461-9426; elane@ap.org \