\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Ends Sharply Dn Despite RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 12:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee closed sharply lower Tuesday but was lifted off a new 21-month low by a statement by the Reserve Bank of India that the adjustment in the value of the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 'adequate,' traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 GMT (5:30 am EST) close of trading Monday the dollar was between 37.39-.41 rupees, up sharply from between 36.88-.89 rupees at the close of trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Tuesday between 36.91-.94 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was traded at a high of 37.52 rupees Tuesday. The last time the dollar traded around these levels was on February 7, 1996. It traded at an all time high of 38.40 rupees in intraday trading on February 6, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI sold an estimated $150 million in the spot market Tuesday after issuing a statement which stopped the fall of the rupee. But only two dealers could confirm having traded with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI bought at 37.50 rupees all the way down to 37.40 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI was asking prices for trades in lots of $10 million. Usually, it trades in lots of $3 million and sometimes in lots of $5 million. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the Reserve Bank of India is estimated to have sold between $100 million and $150 million in outright forward contracts and swaps for six months forward, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to around 37.22-.27 rupees after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement but recovered on demand at lower levels from companies. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, premiums remained firm on steady buying support at lower levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The premium for May-dollars closed between 1.32 rupees and 1.36 rupees, down from a high for the session around 1.50 rupees. It had closed Monday between 1.40 rupees and 1.42 rupees. The premium for October dollars closed between 2.36 rupees and 2.40 rupees, down from between 2.45 rupees and 2.48 rupees Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1113GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbi08spl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
