\par\par \b \uc2  INSTANT VIEW-RBI comment on India rupee adjustment. \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The following are some instant reactions to Reserve Bank of India (RBI) governor's statement on the rupee on Tuesday, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not brook further "overshooting" of the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The RBI governor Chakravarty Rangarajan said on Tuesday an adequate adjustment in the value of the rupee had already taken place and there was no ground for a further weakening. \par \par \uc2  N.S. PARAMASIVAM, HEAD OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  AT ESSAR GROUP \par \par \uc2  The rupee's sharp fall against the dollar on Tuesday morning was largely the result of the market's overreaction. \par \par \uc2  The market over-reacted. It was a combination of interbank (reaction) and moderate corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The market is slightly comforted now after the governor's statement that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) will not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any overshooting of the rupee. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  SHEKHAR SATHE, SENIOR VICE-PRESIDENT, KOTAK MAHINDRA CAPITAL COMPANY \par \par \uc2  I think the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today was a good move. \par \par \uc2  They have released some of the steam which had built up. \par \par \uc2  They really hammered the market at 37.50 so I think this should hold for some time. We are looking at 37.50 holding till March end. \par \par \uc2  But sentiment on the rupee is bearish. We see sentiment on the rupee remaining bearish unless the capital market revives or the economy picks up. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  FREDERICK CASTELLINO, CHIEF DEALER, MECKLAI & MECKLAI \par \par \uc2  The RBI waited upto 37.50 and then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But there is still (dollar) buying pressure. Importers don't seem to be affected much. They think further depreciation (in the rupee) is in store. The market is still bearish on the rupee. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02dc3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
