\par\par \b \uc2  India/Rupee Closes -2: Dlr Seen Close To 37.00 Rupees Tue \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1997\par 12:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday come on the back of sales of $360 million Thursday and another $200 million last Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose above 36.30 rupees on Oct 29 and has been rising continuously after that. \par \par \uc2  That rise has been fueled by an increasingly widely-held belief that the RBI wants the rupee to depreciate slowly in order to lessen the impact on Indian exports of recent depreciations in South-East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The RBI's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are being seen as an effort to slow down the fall of the rupee. In contrast, its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  around two months ago were seen aimed at preventing a fall in the value of the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India is understood to have sold $200 million Tuesday and another $360 million Wednesday to stem the slide of the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This change has led to a rise in demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by companies and importers rushing to cover their unhedged positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they see the dollar moving close to 37.00 rupees Tuesday if the RBI doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily. \par \par \uc2  But several dealers said they didn't expect any strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'It has fallen 13 paise (0.13 rupee) today,' noted one dealer at a state-owned bank. He said he expects the RBI to allow the market to determine the value of the rupee. \par \par \uc2  So long as there isn't too much of volatility, the RBI won't bother \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a senior dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the interbank call rate closed lower after liquidity improved on a lower outflow at the Reserve Bank of India's auction of 14-day treasury bills, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The call rate closed between 4.00% and 4.25%, down from between 6.00% and 6.50% Saturday. \par \par \uc2  For the latest Indian call rates, please see Dow Jones page [57435]. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets\par page [17960].\par -By Pankaj Aher; 91-22-2884211; paher@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1144GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbh08r27\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
