\par\par \b \uc2  India: Rupee Premiums On Fwd Dlrs Lower In Jittery Market \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 07:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--Indian rupee premiums on forward dollars are lower Thursday in a market made jittery after the head of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the 'rupee doesn't reflect fundamentals,' dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The premiums for forward dollars to be delivered at the end of May is between 1.34 rupees and 1.37 rupees, down from Wednesday's close between 1.40 rupees and 1.42 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The premium for October-dollars is between 2.35 rupees and 2.40 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the premiums are slightly up from their opening levels but said few trades have been done at the higher levels. \par \par \uc2  'After the governor's statement, the premiums have to come down,' said a senior dealer at a state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the spot-dollar slipped slightly in morning trading after the RBI Governor, C. Rangarajan, said the RBI 'may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when we find that (the rupee-dollar exchange rate) doesn't reflect the fundamentals of the economy.' He was speaking in Colombo at a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar recovered on the back of a surge in demand at the lower levels and is trading around 36.72 rupees at 0550 GMT (12:50 am EST). \par \par \uc2  Rangarajan also said the country's current account deficit supports a stable rupee. \par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit is around 1% of Gross Domestic Product and the total debt to GDP ratio at about 26% as of March 1997. And India's short-term debt amounts to about 7.4% of total debt. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Thursday between 36.74-.76 rupees then rose immediately and was traded at a high of 36.755 rupees within the first 10 minutes of trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to stabilize around current levels Thursday. Banks will be closed Friday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think the RBI will need to come in today,' said a dealer at a state-owned bank. 'I think they will come in at a higher level now, like 36.80 rupees.' \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets\par page [17960].\par -By Pankaj Aher; 91-22-2884211; paher@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0606GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08p0q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
