\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Up Slightly On RBI Gov Statement, Falls Back \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 05:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee recovered slightly to 36.69 rupees around 0415 GMT (11:15 p.m. EST) on statements by C. Rangarajan, Governor of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the `rupee doesn't reflect fundamentals.' \par \par \uc2  The governor was speaking at a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference in Colombo, the Sri Lankan capital. \par \par \uc2  The governor and the finance minister have been long stressing that the economic fundamentals of the country are sound. \par \par \uc2  The governor said the country's current account deficit supports a stable rupee. \par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit is around only 1% of gross domestic product and the total debt to GDP ratio at about 26% as of March 1997. And India's short term debt amounts to about 7.4% of total debt. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar recovered to trade around 36.72 rupees a few minutes after the statement. \par \par \uc2  At 0430 GMT (11:30 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading between 36.71 rupees and 36.72 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened higher against the dollar Thursday as banks continued to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively despite heavy dollar-sales by the Reserve Bank of India in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of India in the previous session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Thursday between 36.74-36.76 rupees then rose immediately and was traded at a high of 36.755 rupees within the first 10 minutes of trading. \par \par \uc2  For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [17960]. \par \par \uc2  -By Pankaj Aher; 91-22-2884211; paher@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0441GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08ot4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
