\par\par \b \uc2  India: Rupee Dn Against Dlr Midday, But Off New 20-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 08:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow  Jones)--The Indian rupee is down against the dollar in midday trading Thursday, but off the new 20-month low it set earlier in the session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0640 GMT (01:40 a.m. EST), the dollar is trading between 36.73-.74 rupees, down from its high of 36.755 rupees in early trading. It had closed between 36.69-.70 rupees Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to trade around current levels for the rest of the session. Banks are closed Friday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The market seems to have stabilized a little after Wednesday's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a statement Thursday by the governor, C. Rangarajan, said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  'repeatedly and aggressively' in the market Wednesday to break the rupee's fall. Several dealers estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $300 million Wednesday, the bulk of it in the forward market, but some dealers estimate the figure to be closer to $400 million. \par \par \uc2  The RBI had also sold an estimated $50 million to $100 million Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had slipped below 36.70 rupees briefly in morning trading after Rangarajan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the 'rupee doesn't reflect fundamentals.' \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar recovered on continued demand from companies. \par \par \uc2  Rangarajan, who was speaking at a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference in Colombo, also said the country's current account deficit supports a stable rupee. \par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit is around 1% of Gross Domestic Product and the total debt to GDP ratio is at about 26% as of March 1997. And India's short term debt amounts to about 7.4% of total debt. \par \par \uc2  But one dealer at a large U.S. bank said he discounted the impact of the governor's statement. 'There was so much activity yesterday, everyone is sitting out today,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Volumes are down to almost a third of that traded Wednesday, he said. \par \par \uc2  'If you look at what has happened in the last three weeks, we have a steady depreciation of the rupee managed by the mechanics of the market and not a devaluation,' he said. \par \par \uc2  'They are happy with that. Or else they would have hit the market hard. If you remember, last time (the dollar) touched 36.70 rupees, they took it down to 36.58 rupes in one day,' he said. \par \par \uc2  For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [17960]. \par \par \uc2  -By Pankaj Aher; 91-22-2884211; paher@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0707GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbd08mt8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
