\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  RBI's verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  slows rupee's fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended Thursday weaker at 36.75/76 to the dollar compared with 36.71/74 opening and the previous close of 36.69/71, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrested the pace of the rupee's weakening, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was only a token \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened at 36.71/74 and soon fell to 36.75, the 21-month low the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had touched on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A statement by the Reserve Bank of India governor (RBI) at a South Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers conference at Colombo triggered an immediate recovery in the spot rupee, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  RBI governor Chakravarty Rangarajan told the conference, market players should take economic fundamentals into account and not overreact to gossip and rumours lest they hurt themselves. \par \par \uc2  "The most important concern for the central bankers in the present scenario is the overreaction of the market participants which sometimes takes the form of contagion effects," Rangarajan told the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the remarks, though aimed at the wider Asian audience, triggered a rupee rally which lasted until noon, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee recovered to 36.70/71 levels after the remark and was stuck at 36.73/74 level until afternoon when the underlying dollar demand began asserting itself, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was trading nervously at 36.75 towards the close but there was no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "They are not opposed to depreciation but they don't want too sharp a fall too soon," said a public sector bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "They want to ensure a smooth descent," he said. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums opened lower for most maturities but rose in the absence of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and genuine corporate demand, dealers said. RBI had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in forwards on Wednesday, pulling down the premiums. \par \par \uc2  Premiums closed Thursday sharply higher than the previous close, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The six month annualised forward premium closed at 7.67 percent compared with the previous close of 7.15 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbd02mr7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
