\par\par \b \uc2  Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to stop rupee rot. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell sharply against the dollar on importer demand on Wednesday, triggering aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI sold about $200 million on Tuesday to cushion the rupee's decline and even more on Wednesday after the rupee sank to a low of 36.75 to the dollar in a fast market. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid (\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  becoming) another victim of the Asian markets contagion," said a senior dealer at Societe Generale bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  The rupee settled around 36.71 in late trading on Wednesday, marking a 1.5 percent depreciation since markets in Asia began plunging three weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  While the scale of the decline pales beside other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Indian importers, anticipating further falls, scrambled for dollar cover as signs of weakness materialised. \par \par \uc2  "Importers are in the market seeking cover," a dealer at a leading Bombay bank said. "Earlier, they would never book forward -- they would wait till the last day of the LC (letter of credit)." \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Wednesday at 36.65/67 against the dollar compared with the previous close of 36.63/65. \par \par \uc2  RBI dollar sales mounted when the rupee breached a key level at 36.70, but the market absorbed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money and the rupee's recovery was fragile, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They (the RBI) are selling whenever it touches 36.73/74 level," said a public sector bank dealer. "They seem to be comfortable with 36.70 for today." \par \par \uc2  The RBI had been a net buyer of dollars until August and turned into a net seller the following month. \par \par \uc2  Treasury managers said a series of developments in recent weeks put the rupee in the firing line. \par \par \uc2  Worries about a slowdown in capital inflows into India followed in the wake of the Asian markets crisis. \par \par \uc2  An $800 million global depositary receipt (GDR) issue of the state-run Gas Authority of India Ltd (GAIL) was deferred earlier this month as investors backed away from emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  Newspapers on Wednesday said a planned GDR issue for another state-run firm, Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Ltd (MTNL), could suffer the same fate, although the government said no decision had been taken on a postponement. \par \par \uc2  Investor disenchantment with emerging markets also sent the Bombay stock market reeling on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bombay Stock Exchange top 30 index fell 2.3 percent to a seven-month low of 3,637.77, down 85.63 points, as foreign funds accelerated selling to meet redemption pressures. \par \par \uc2  A statement by RBI Governor Chakravarty Rangarajan last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if there was a "high degree" of volatility in exchange markets was interpreted by dealers as a sign the bank would not mind a weaker rupee. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: bombay.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbc02khd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
