\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee bends on dlr demand in holiday market. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee closed for the weekend weaker against the dollar after brief fluctuation early on Friday, baffling bankers' expectations that activity would be dampened by the holiday season, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We are so used to a static rupee that small volatilities make headlines," said a dealer at a public sector bank soon after the nation's largest commercial bank bought dollars aggressively in early trade. \par \par \uc2  He said Indian firms and banks should get used to two way movements depending on day-to-day factors. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Friday steady at 36.31/32, but large purchases by the state-run State Bank of India (SBI) caught the market offguard, and dragged the rupee to 36.41 -- a drop of 0.10 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Throughout the recent turmoil in East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been relatively stable, losing roughly half a percentage point to 36.40 from 36.20 over the last ten days. \par \par \uc2  That it maintained this level without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely seen as an achievement, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was little demand on Friday from any source besides the SBI. "The rupee recovered only after SBI dropped its purchase price below the 36.40 level," one dealer at an Indian bank told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) checked prices but did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Yet the rupee failed to entirely make up its losses in a thin market, since inflows from corporates were blocked by the holidays to mark Diwali, the Hindu festival of lights. \par \par \uc2  "Banks were long on dollars," said a senior dealer at a foreign bank. "They went and offered (dollars) to SBI (after SBI had stopped bidding)," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed SBI's demand to month-end dollar payments on behalf of public sector companies. \par \par \uc2  Fund managers who have invested in Indian stock markets said the rupee's stability was a source of comfort. \par \par \uc2  "It's very consoling that the rupee has remained virtually unmoved throughout the crisis," said an official with an overseas fund manager. \par \par \uc2  The inter-bank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market saw minor convulsions but the rupee recovered quickly when fears of repatriation by foreign funds proved unfounded, bank dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) recent assurance that it was watching the situation and would ensure that orderly conditions prevailed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers saw the rupee weaken gradually over the next few months. \par \par \uc2  "India's plan to liberalise gold imports should lower the premium on the yellow metal in the country and boost imports, simultaneously boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  India's appetite for bullion is among the world's largest. \par \par \uc2  Another factor is Indian firms' increasing preference for domestic debt compared to offshore debt, facilitated by falling domestic interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Offshore debt has been one of the important sources of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months. \par \par \uc2  But falling interest rates have prompted some of India's leading firms to fund new projects through domestic issues instead of the offshore loans they originally envisaged. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtav03cqo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
