\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Closes Dn Vs Dlr; Banks Cover Earlier Dlr Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 1997\par 12:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee closed weaker against the dollar Friday on dollar-buying by banks covering earlier dollar sales, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said these banks sold dollars when the dollar rose sharply in early trading Friday on buying by State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  At 1030 GMT (5:30 a.m. EST), the close of trading, the dollar was quoted between 36.3650-.3750 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Friday at 36.2900-.3200 rupees, little changed from its Wednesday's close at 36.3000-.3200 rupees, but in early trade moved up to a day's high of 36.4200. \par \par \uc2  'State Bank's was the best bid (for the dollar) on Friday,' said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that State Bank also sold dollars around 36.4200 after initially buying all the way from 36.30 to 36.38 rupees in several bouts early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the foreign bank said the dollar is expected to range between 36.3000-.4200 rupees next week. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar rise will be capped around 36.4000-.4200 rupees because the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels,' said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had given indications to this effect in its 'strong comments last week,' while referring to the rupee in the background of the turbulence in the stock markets around the world. \par \par \uc2  On Oct. 28, the RBI said that 'the impact of this (global developments) on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is not likely to be significant.' \par \par \uc2  'The rupee should, therefore, remain stable and the RBI will ensure orderly conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market,' the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its statement. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES INDIA REPORT  31-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1142GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011005dtav0016g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
