\par\par \b \uc2  India: Rupee Closes Up On Absence Of Large Dlr Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1997\par 13:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee closed stronger Thursday because there wasn't any major dollar buying by banks except State Bank of India, which lowered its bidding rate throughout the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 GMT (6:30 a.m. EDT) close of trading Thursday the dollar was between 36.2100-.2200 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Thursday between 36.2300-.2400 rupees, slightly higher from Wednesday's close of between 36.2250-.2300 rupees. \par \par \uc2  'There was very thin trading in the market near close of trading,' said a dealer at a state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  She said increased dollar inflows from banks pushed even State Bank to sell part of their dollar purchases. However, most dealers said they didn't see State Bank selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'I didn't see any dollar sales by the State Bank (throughout the day),' said a dealer at a British bank. \par \par \uc2  State Bank, India's largest commercial bank, has been the major dollar buyer this week. Some dealers expect the bank to continue buying dollars at lower levels Friday. \par \par \uc2  State Bank was offered the dollar by several bank Thursday morning at around 36.2300 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the British bank said several banks were selling small amounts of dollars. This pushed down the dollar near close of trading. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer at a European bank also confirmed that he didn't see any dollar selling by State Bank. \par \par \uc2  He said that he expected the dollar to range at between 36.2050-.2350 rupees Friday. \par \par \uc2  'There will be a bit of pressure on the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars (at below 36.2000 rupees),' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1151GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtag07qio\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
