\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee ends steady, RBI in token  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 29 (Reuter) - The rupee closed Monday steady against the dollar as a token \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards the close went largely unnoticed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened steady at 36.19/20 and moved in a narrow range thorughout the day, dealers said. It closed at 36.18/19. \par \par \uc2  The opening quote was the rupee's lowest point on Monday. \par \par \uc2  It touched a day's high of 36.17 in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Moderate dollar demand from the State Bank of India (SBI) and a few others sustained the dollar at this level, a dealer at a public sector bank said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee would have ended around the same level even without Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI stepped in near the close and bought very small amounts - estimated at about $10 million - from a handful of public sector banks in Bombay, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They bought $3.0 million from us at 36.19 at closing time," a dealer at a public sector bank in Bombay said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign and major Indian public sector banks which are normally hit by the RBI were spared today, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If they hit foreign banks, it will be easily absorbed," said the chief dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  He said RBI wanted to achieve its objective -- that it wanted the rupee to continue at the current level -- through relatively cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hence the selection of low profile public sector banks. \par \par \uc2  RBI governor Chakravarty Rangarajan said in a television interview on Saturday the rupee can and will continue to remain stable at the current levels. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe they (the RBI) wanted to pre-empt (the effect) of any month-end (spurt in dollar) demand," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be largely inactive on Tuesday as banks are closed for customer transactions. \par \par \uc2  Banks are again closed on October 2 for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said there was no doubt about the rupee was set to extend its gains over the dollar in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds continued to be net buyers on Indian stock markets and there were good dollar inflows from other channels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI is controlling the market very well," said Sharukh Wadia, chief dealer at Standard Chartered Bank, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's double-edged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy designed to check a sharp rise as well as fall in the rupee's value. \par \par \uc2  He expected the rupee to gradually gain in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  Forward dollar premiums continued to ease on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The six month annualised premium closed Monday at 5.54 percent compared with the previous close of 5.60 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom (91)22-265 9000, Fax 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9t01yn9\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ad